\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Scatter plots of economic vs.\ humanitarian costs (both as \% of GDP) under three mental health cost models. Black dots: linear (baseline); blue triangles: concave (saturation); red squares: convex (threshold). The three sets of points overlap closely in all four regions, confirming that the efficient frontier is insensitive to the functional form of the mental health cost model.}}{54}{figure.caption.39}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mh_scatter}{{9}{54}{Scatter plots of economic vs.\ humanitarian costs (both as \% of GDP) under three mental health cost models. Black dots: linear (baseline); blue triangles: concave (saturation); red squares: convex (threshold). The three sets of points overlap closely in all four regions, confirming that the efficient frontier is insensitive to the functional form of the mental health cost model}{figure.caption.39}{}}
